.TH "ELEMENT.GOTPOINTERCAPTURE_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Element.gotpointercapture_event \- Element: gotpointercapture event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]gotpointercapture\f[B]\f[R] event is fired when an
element captures a pointer using \f[CR]setPointerCapture()\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqgotpointercapture\(dq, (event) => { })

ongotpointercapture = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]PointerEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
This example gets a \f[CR]<p>\f[R] element and listens for the
\f[CR]gotpointercapture\f[R] event.
It then calls \f[CR]setPointerCapture()\f[R] on the element on a
\f[CR]pointerdown\f[R] event, which will trigger
\f[CR]gotpointercapture\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] para = document.querySelector(\(dqp\(dq);

para.addEventListener(\(dqgotpointercapture\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(dqI\(aqve been captured!\(dq);
});

para.addEventListener(\(dqpointerdown\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  para.setPointerCapture(event.pointerId);
});
.EE
.PP
The same example, using the \f[CR]ongotpointercapture\f[R] event handler
property:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] para = document.querySelector(\(dqp\(dq);

para.ongotpointercapture = () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(dqI\(aqve been captured!\(dq);
};

para.addEventListener(\(dqpointerdown\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  para.setPointerCapture(event.pointerId);
});
.EE
